# Mobile Surface Flattening (RINK Tank)

Desktop may keep a clear card hierarchy. **Mobile must not stack Card-in-Card.**

## System

Use `styles/layout-surfaces.css` + `Card` props:

| Role | When | Mobile behavior |
|------|------|-----------------|
| `surface="primary"` | One dominant block (drill screen, main setup card) | Keeps chrome, tighter padding |
| `surface="section"` | Page sections (Account blocks, dashboard widgets) | Flattens to section + divider |
| `surface="nested"` | Inner panels inside a primary/section | Fully flat |
| `surface="inline"` | Light tint / hint blocks | Fully flat |
| `ui-flat-panel` | Non-Card panels (setup live/import panels) | Loses padding/border chrome |
| `ui-page-shell` | Page root | Consistent gap + consecutive section dividers |

Legacy aliases still work: `primary-card`, `mobile-flatten`, `mobile-flatten-card`.

## Rules

1. **Do not** fix “too nested on mobile” by shrinking fonts or adding more wrappers.
2. **Do** assign a surface role when creating/editing layout.
3. On mobile, group with **section titles, dividers, spacing, subtle tints** — not a fourth card.
4. Keep **Desktop** visual hierarchy unless the change is intentionally shared.
5. Tables that crush on mobile need a **stacked companion** (`.ui-stat-stack` / `.ui-table-hide-mobile`), not tinier columns.

## Prefer

```tsx
<div className="ui-page-shell">
  <Card surface="primary">…</Card>
  <Card surface="section">…</Card>
</div>
```

Inside a primary block:

```tsx
<section className="ui-content-section">
  <h3 className="ui-section-title">Mission</h3>
  …
</section>
```

or `<Card surface="nested">` / `className="mobile-flatten-card"`.
